          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they feel content, but they may also purr to self-soothe when stressed or
              recovering. Context matters: relaxed posture and slow blinking usually point to comfort, while
              hiding or tension can signal that your cat needs reassurance or a veterinary checkup.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
